ient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts and waits longer before each retry.\n\n- **Wait times:** `backoff * 2**attempt`, so 0.5s and then 1s with the default. You can change the base delay with the new `backoff=0.5` constructor argument.\n- **When it retries:** only on 503. Any other HTTP error is raised straight away. If all 3 attempts get 503, the last 503 error is raised.\n- **Network errors:** timeouts and refused connections are not retried, because that's outside what you asked for.\n\nI tested it against a real local HTTP server:\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests |\n|---|---|---|\n| 200 straight away | data returned | 1 |\n| 503, 503, then 200 | data returned | 3 |\n| 503 three times | 503 error raised | 3 |\n| 500 | 500 error raised | 1 |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add one.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 71284, "requests_cache_write": 107156, "requests_cost_usd": 0.5815448000000001, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1573, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial13", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 84, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:49:02.702746+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 37.199, "t_checker_s": 1.926, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1585, "tokens_cache_read": 71284, "tokens_cache_write": 107156, "tokens_fresh": 1585, "tokens_input_unc